Joy of Computing – Week 1 Debrief
1. Introduction
The Week 1 Debrief is a Quality Circle session where students discuss and reflect on what they learned from the NPTEL Week 1 videos. Instead of introducing new concepts, the class focuses on sharing ideas, asking questions, and learning from one another.

Key Points
No new topics are taught.

Discussion-based class instead of a lecture.

Every student must participate.

Learning is based on reflection and interaction.


2. Things to Bring
Before coming to class, every student should prepare the following:

Requirements
One Question from the Week 1 videos.

One "Wow" Moment (the most surprising or interesting concept learned).

Both should be written down.

Evaluation
Attendance

Activity Marks

Quiz Performance


3. Operation Sequence (Quality Circle Protocol)
OP 10 – Wow Wall (≈12 Minutes)
Students work in pairs and write their biggest "Wow" from Week 1 on the board.

Objectives

Share interesting discoveries.

Encourage deeper thinking.

Avoid repeating ideas.

Key Points

One unique "Wow" per pair.

Later pairs must think beyond previous answers.

Promotes creativity and observation.


OP 20 – Question Exchange (≈15 Minutes)
Each student passes their written question two seats to the left and attempts to answer the new question before the class discussion.

Objectives

Improve problem-solving skills.

Learn from classmates.

Encourage independent thinking.

Key Points

Read the received question carefully.

Attempt an answer first.

Compare your answer during the class discussion.


OP 30 – Instructor Synthesis (≈10 Minutes)
The instructor summarizes the discussion and connects all important ideas from Week 1.

Objectives

Clear misunderstandings.

Explain the core message of Week 1.

Show how the topics relate to future lessons.

Key Points

Review important concepts.

Connect different student responses.

Prepare students for upcoming weeks.


OP 40 – Activity: The 7-Check Challenge (≈12 Minutes)
Students play "Find the Faulty Station" as a class and then in pairs.

Objectives

Understand Binary Search (Half-Splitting).

Compare efficient and inefficient search methods.

Key Points

Divide the problem into halves.

Eliminate half of the possibilities after each check.

Locate the faulty station in only 7 checks instead of 100.

Activity carries 10 marks.


OP 50 – Quiz (≈8 Minutes)
A short quiz is conducted on Week 1 concepts.

Topics Covered

Algorithms

Sequence

Loops

If/Else Statements

Jobs 01–02

Purpose

Check conceptual understanding.

Reinforce classroom learning.


OP 60 – Dispatch (≈3 Minutes)
The instructor gives instructions for the next week.

Key Tasks

Create an EduBlocks account.

Understand next week's assignments.

Prepare for the transition from block programming to text-based Python beginning with Job 04.



